<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description> (255-char cap), and it is INSIDE
        the root element on purpose - a comment ABOVE <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy.

        THE _Count__c SUFFIX IS REQUIRED HERE FOR A WEAKER REASON THAN ON ITS SIBLING, AND
        THAT IS PRECISELY WHY IT MUST NOT BE DROPPED. `Fields_Missing__c` is not literally
        rule 4's Boolean shape the way Fields_Captured__c is - "Missing" reads as a STATE -
        but it sits directly beside a field that IS that shape, so a reader who resolves
        one as a Boolean resolves the other the same way. Naming the pair inconsistently is
        worse than naming either one wrongly. Full argument on the Lead twin.

        DERIVED BUT STORED: missing = 9 - captured, always. It carries no information its
        sibling does not; it exists so a report can filter "deals whose intake was missing
        three or more facts" without arithmetic in the report. It costs nothing - all three
        values are computed in one pass on the Lead and carried in the same conversion
        update.

        CARRIED, NOT RECOMPUTED. It describes the ORIGINAL broker email, not the current
        state of this deal record. Someone filling in the guidance price by hand does not
        move it, and that is correct.

        NULL means not scored (fail-soft); zero missing means a COMPLETE extraction - the
        best possible answer, not the absence of one.
    -->
    <fullName>Fields_Missing_Count__c</fullName>
    <description>How many of the nine signed-off deal-process extraction keys were NOT captured from the original broker email, carried from the Lead at conversion. Always nine minus Fields Captured Count. Zero means a complete extraction.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <inlineHelpText>Count of deal facts the automated extraction did not find in the original broker email, out of nine. Zero means nothing was missing.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Fields Missing Count</label>
    <precision>3</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Number</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
